if (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development') {
  const axios = require('axios');
  module.exports = axios;
} else {
  module.exports = http;
}
```

### Summary

- Use conditional imports or environment checks to include the HTTP client only in development.
- Configure your build tool to exclude dev-only code from production bundles.
- Leverage tree shaking and modern bundler features to minimize bundle size.
- Keep dev-specific code isolated and well-documented.

By following these strategies, you can safely use an HTTP client library during development without shipping it to production.

